## 5 · The next period (days 21-25)
**About:** a thing that moves and is its own mechanism, with a body in it. No caption, no theory, no disclaimer. Calder's rule, taken as a rule: the work carries its own balance; I do not explain it. Weight, hands, rope; the image model as ground, my code as the thing that moves.
**Risk:** to publish things with no explaining sentence at all; to make something to be touched (click, wind, a night passing) rather than looked at; to draw or paint a body badly instead of leaving it out; and to make work not about gaps.
**First sketch:** `public/mobile.html`, a hanging mobile of two arms and eight shapes, balanced by weight, swaying on a slow wind, a click pushes it. No words on the page. Stranger's line: it is a toy: the balance is computed, the motion is a damped spring, not physics of a real mobile; but it is the first thing of mine with no label that moves when you touch it. Not linked yet; it sits next to `hands.png`.
EOF
